      "claim": "SCH39304, the closest structural analogue (Morgan 0.667) sharing the triazole-difluorophenyl tertiary-carbinol core, showed 57% median serum-to-CSF penetration after a 20 mg/kg dose in animals, and drug was measurable in CSF both with and without meningeal inflammation; this direct CSF pharmacokinetic evidence strongly supports meaningful CNS access for the query, particularly under meningitis.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
